---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Layout title="Equipnivo licence help | Activate & move your licence" description="Activate your Equipnivo licence in Settings → Licence. One licence covers one server installation, with unlimited staff and offline use after activation.">
<section class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">EQUIPNIVO / LICENCE HELP</p><h1 class="page-title">From Trial to Full.<br />A few simple steps.</h1><p class="lead narrow">Activate on your main PC with an internet connection. After that, Equipnivo works offline on your local network.</p><div class="two-columns"><article class="instruction-panel"><h2>Activate your purchase</h2><ol class="steps"><li><a href={site.checkout}>Purchase Equipnivo for £79.</a></li><li>Receive and copy the full licence key supplied with your purchase.</li><li>Open Equipnivo on the main PC and sign in as an Admin.</li><li>Go to <strong>Settings → Licence</strong>.</li><li>Enter the key and activate while connected to the internet.</li><li>Equipnivo becomes <strong>Full</strong>. The equipment limit is removed and the licence works offline afterwards.</li></ol></article><article><h2>One installation. Unlimited people.</h2><p>One licence allows one active Equipnivo server installation. Phones, tablets and laptops connecting as staff clients do not use up licences.</p><h3>Moving to another PC</h3><p>Deactivate the old server as an Admin before activating your key on the new PC. Move or back up your local maintenance data separately; licence activation does not transfer the database.</p><h3>Keep your key safe</h3><p>Keep a private copy of your purchase details and licence key. Enter the key inside Equipnivo on your main PC.</p><h3>Still preparing your installation?</h3><p><a class="text-link" href="/download/">Check Windows download status and getting started →</a></p></article></div></section>
</Layout>
